    <GaugingStation location="Darlaston" name="Trent" number="28083">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Rated station gauging a relatively urban catchment near Stoke-on-Trent.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Multipath ultrasonic gauge installed beneath A34 road bridge on a gentle curve. Ultrasonic gauge replaced with a new NivuFlow time of flight setup in February 2022. However, peak flow data are from three peak flow ratings applied across period of record, derived for flood forecasting. Out-of-bank flows inferred by the rated flow from spot gaugings. Site experiences large silt deposits on left bank due to upstream bend in the river. This can affect ultrasonic performance though is managed. High flow ADCP gaugings carried out using a rope from the road bridge. Low flow gaugings carried out in the ultrasonic section using remote controlled ADCP.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Time-of-flight ultrasonic installed at the site, however, peak flow data are from ratings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">AMAX levels in water years 1985/86 and 1986/87 are suspect, but AMAX and daily mean flow magnitudes are consistent with analogue station 28040 upstream. Station undermined in 1987 flood, reconstructed 1990/1. In 2001-2002, gauge not performing v well. Transducers failing constantly, especially lower ones (due to silt). Problems in 2002-2003 with rubble in channel now creating skew flows &amp; siltation. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Quite responsive but flow regime dominated by Strongford WRW discharge (Stoke-on-Trent).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Moderate relief catchment, substantially urbanised with Stoke-on-Trent and Newcastle-under-Lyme. Geology mainly Coal Measures and Marls, Millstone Grit and subordinate Sherwood S'st, widely covered by Boulder Clay. Mining, industrial and mixed agricultural land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Well gauged to QMED, albeit with a lot of scatter." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Uncertainty caused by scatter in gaugings limits suitability for Pooling, despite gaugings above QMED fitting the rating well." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
